{
  "id": "temporal-construal-theory",
  "term": "temporal construal theory",
  "definition": "Temporal construal theory is the idea that how people think about a choice changes with its psychological distance in time. Decisions about the distant future are framed more abstractly and in terms of broad, central features, while decisions about the near future rely more on concrete, immediate details.",
